## What changed in this file, and when

The previous version of these instructions targeted **v1.27**, which left
support in 2024. More importantly, the install script pointed at
`apt.kubernetes.io` and `packages.cloud.google.com`. Those repositories were
frozen in September 2023 and switched off in March 2024, so the script
failed at `apt update` for anyone who ran it after that date.

The replacement is `pkgs.k8s.io`. Two things about it are worth knowing:

- The repository URL contains the **minor version**. `apt upgrade` will never
  move you from 1.36 to 1.37; you edit `/etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list`
  first. This is deliberate, and it is the part people get wrong.
- Keys go in `/etc/apt/keyrings` with `signed-by=`, not `apt-key` or
  `/etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d`. A key in `trusted.gpg.d` is trusted for *every*
  repository on the machine.
